# project: new_elective_course
// Launch a new elective course at the university next academic year.

-> draft_syllabus

=== draft_syllabus ===
Draft the syllabus for the new elective course.
Done when a complete syllabus is ready to submit to the curriculum committee.
+ [Submit syllabus to the committee] -> committee_review

=== committee_review ===
The department curriculum committee reviews the syllabus.
It can send it back for revision as many times as needed.
+ [Send back for revision] @human ~loop~ -> draft_syllabus
+ [Committee endorses the syllabus] @human -> dean_approval

=== dean_approval ===
The dean gives final approval of the committee-endorsed syllabus.
+ [Dean approves the course] @human -> enrollment_listing
+ [Dean requires changes] @human ~loop~ -> draft_syllabus

=== enrollment_listing ===
The approved course is listed for enrollment.
At the registration deadline, check how many students have enrolled.
* [Twelve or more students enrolled by the deadline] -> prepare_materials
* [Fewer than twelve students enrolled by the deadline] -> low_enrollment_decision

=== low_enrollment_decision ===
Enrollment came in under twelve; the department head decides how to proceed.
* [Run it anyway as a seminar] @human -> prepare_materials
* [Defer the course a year] @human -> deferred

=== deferred ===
The course is deferred to the following academic year; the approved syllabus stays on file.
-> END

=== prepare_materials ===
Prepare course materials over the summer.
Done when lectures, assignments and assessments are ready for the semester.
* [Materials ready for the semester] -> teach_semester

=== teach_semester ===
Teach the course for the semester and collect student evaluations.
* [Semester complete, evaluations collected] -> course_review_board

=== course_review_board ===
The course review board examines the evaluations and decides the course's future.
* [Make it a permanent offering] @human -> permanent_offering
* [Do not continue the course] @human -> END

=== permanent_offering ===
The course joins the catalogue as a permanent elective offering.
-> END
